<title>SINGAPORE: Econ 1996/97 net profit rises 48.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Econ 1996/97 net profit rises 48.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>(millions of Singapore dollars unless specified)</p>
<p>    Net profit				   8.13 vs   5.46</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)			 5.00 vs   7.50</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)			5.10 vs   4.00</p>
<p>    Group share fully diluted (cents)    3.30 vs   3.20</p>
<p>    Turnover				   302.52 vs 274.76</p>
<p>    Investment income			  0.12 vs   0.13</p>
<p>    Other income				 0.78 vs   0.50</p>
<p>    Interest expense			   4.75 vs   5.09</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	     12.84 vs   8.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    10.68 vs  11.40</p>
<p>    Income from associates		   3.06 vs   0.25 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax					    5.40 vs   5.58</p>
<p>    Minority loss				0.21 vs   0.11</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss			 0.50 vs   5.40</p>
<p>    Last day books open:	   September 26, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Econ International Ltd is a construction and infrastructure materials company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
